{"slug":"/students/subjects/physics/mechanics/momentum/","source":"students/subjects/physics/mechanics/momentum.html","area":"students","kind":"content","title":"Momentum & Impulse | Physics Mechanics","description":"","subject":"physics","body":"<div class=\"max-w-6xl mx-auto\">\n        <nav class=\"mb-8\">\n            <a href=\"/students/subjects/physics/mechanics/\" class=\"text-blue-600 hover:text-blue-700\">← Back to Mechanics</a>\n        </nav>\n\n        <div class=\"content-card rounded-xl p-8\">\n            <header class=\"mb-12\">\n                <h1 class=\"text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Momentum &amp; Impulse</h1>\n                <p class=\"text-lg text-gray-600\">Understanding momentum, conservation laws, and impulse in collisions</p>\n            </header>\n\n            <div class=\"grid gap-8\">\n                <!-- Linear Momentum -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Linear Momentum</h2>\n                    <div class=\"space-y-6\">\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n                                <div>\n                                    <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Definition</h3>\n                                    <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                        <li>• p = mv (mass × velocity)</li>\n                                        <li>• Vector quantity</li>\n                                        <li>• Units: kg⋅m/s</li>\n                                        <li>• Direction same as velocity</li>\n                                    </ul>\n                                </div>\n                                <div>\n                                    <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Properties</h3>\n                                    <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                        <li>• Conserved in closed systems</li>\n                                        <li>• Changes with force application</li>\n                                        <li>• Important in collisions</li>\n                                        <li>• Depends on reference frame</li>\n                                    </ul>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Conservation of Momentum -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Conservation of Momentum</h2>\n                    <div class=\"space-y-6\">\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Principle</h3>\n                            <p class=\"text-gray-700 mb-4\">Total momentum of an isolated system remains constant if no external forces act on it.</p>\n                            \n                            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n                                <div>\n                                    <h4 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">Mathematical Form</h4>\n                                    <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                        <li>• p₁ + p₂ = p₁' + p₂'</li>\n                                        <li>• Before collision = After collision</li>\n                                        <li>• Vector sum important</li>\n                                        <li>• Valid in all directions</li>\n                                    </ul>\n                                </div>\n                                <div>\n                                    <h4 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-2\">Applications</h4>\n                                    <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                        <li>• Collisions</li>\n                                        <li>• Explosions</li>\n                                        <li>• Rocket propulsion</li>\n                                        <li>• Nuclear reactions</li>\n                                    </ul>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Impulse -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Impulse</h2>\n                    <div class=\"space-y-6\">\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n                                <div>\n                                    <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Definition</h3>\n                                    <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                        <li>• J = F⋅Δt</li>\n                                        <li>• J = Δp (change in momentum)</li>\n                                        <li>• Units: N⋅s</li>\n                                        <li>• Vector quantity</li>\n                                    </ul>\n                                </div>\n                                <div>\n                                    <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Applications</h3>\n                                    <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                        <li>• Safety features</li>\n                                        <li>• Sports equipment</li>\n                                        <li>• Vehicle collisions</li>\n                                        <li>• Impact force reduction</li>\n                                    </ul>\n                                </div>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Types of Collisions -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Types of Collisions</h2>\n                    <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6\">\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Elastic Collisions</h3>\n                            <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                <li>• Momentum conserved</li>\n                                <li>• Kinetic energy conserved</li>\n                                <li>• Perfect rebound</li>\n                                <li>• Example: Atomic collisions</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Inelastic Collisions</h3>\n                            <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                <li>• Momentum conserved</li>\n                                <li>• Energy lost to heat/sound</li>\n                                <li>• Objects separate</li>\n                                <li>• Example: Car crashes</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                            <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Perfectly Inelastic</h3>\n                            <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                <li>• Momentum conserved</li>\n                                <li>• Maximum energy loss</li>\n                                <li>• Objects stick together</li>\n                                <li>• Example: Clay collision</li>\n                            </ul>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Practical Applications -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Practical Applications</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <div class=\"grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6\">\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Safety Design</h3>\n                                <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                    <li>• Car crumple zones</li>\n                                    <li>• Airbags</li>\n                                    <li>• Sports padding</li>\n                                    <li>• Protective equipment</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div>\n                            <div>\n                                <h3 class=\"font-medium text-gray-800 mb-3\">Sports Technology</h3>\n                                <ul class=\"space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700\">\n                                    <li>• Ball design</li>\n                                    <li>• Racket technology</li>\n                                    <li>• Impact analysis</li>\n                                    <li>• Performance optimization</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </div>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Practice Problems -->\n                <section>\n                    <h2 class=\"text-xl font-semibold text-gray-800 mb-4\">Practice Problems</h2>\n                    <div class=\"bg-white/50 rounded-lg p-6\">\n                        <ol class=\"list-decimal pl-6 space-y-4 text-gray-700\">\n                            <li>\n                                <p class=\"font-medium mb-2\">Conservation of Momentum</p>\n                                <p>Two objects of masses 2kg and 3kg collide. Initial velocities are 4m/s and -2m/s respectively. If they stick together, find final velocity.</p>\n                            </li>\n                            <li>\n                                <p class=\"font-medium mb-2\">Impulse</p>\n                                <p>A 0.5kg ball hits a wall at 10m/s and rebounds at 8m/s. Calculate:</p>\n                                <ul class=\"list-disc pl-6 mt-2 space-y-1 text-sm\">\n                                    <li>Change in momentum</li>\n                                    <li>Impulse</li>\n                                    <li>Average force if contact time is 0.01s</li>\n                                </ul>\n                            </li>\n                            <li>\n                                <p class=\"font-medium mb-2\">Elastic Collision</p>\n                                <p>Two identical masses undergo an elastic collision. If one is initially at rest, prove that they exchange velocities.</p>\n                            </li>\n                        </ol>\n                    </div>\n                </section>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n<!-- Topic Quiz System -->","bodyClass":"min-h-screen bg-gradient-to-br from-blue-50 to-indigo-100 p-6","bodyStyle":"","css":["body { font-family: 'Inter', sans-serif; }\n        .content-card {\n            -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(16px);\n            backdrop-filter: blur(16px);\n            background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.7);\n            border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n            box-shadow: 0 8px 32px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);\n        }"],"quiz":null,"tracker":null,"links":[]}